# nr-office-comrs-word-edit: the Word editor of mixdog-office-com (src/word/edit/{mod,author,formatting,lists,append,text,styles,review,structure,
# template,tables}.rs), tests/word_edit.rs, tests/word_edit_live.rs, recorder/scenarios/word-edit.json and tests/fixtures/word-edit/inputs/pixel.png.
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave); every file was checked to parse with rustfmt only.
# No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name and no Cargo.lock change belong to this task (it uses `regex`, already a dependency of the crate).
# Depends on nr-office-comrs-word-read being applied first (src/lib.rs `pub mod word;` and the readers table of src/drivers.rs, see its fragment).

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/word/mod.rs (owned by nr-office-comrs-word-read)
After the line `pub(crate) mod edit;` add the public path the drivers table and the tests use:

    pub use edit::Editor;

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/drivers.rs (not owned by this task)
Fill the editors table:

    static EDITORS: &[(&str, &dyn FormatEditor)] = &[("docx", &crate::word::Editor)];

(`operation_names()` of the editor answers the 41 names of the docx list of tests/fixtures/registry/operations.json; the other two formats add their own
line when their tasks are applied.)

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test targets, after `[[test]] name = "word_read_live"`:

    [[test]]
    name = "word_edit"
    path = "tests/word_edit.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "word_edit_live"
    path = "tests/word_edit_live.rs"

## 4. What the lead should know
- tests/word_edit.rs runs against a scripted Word object model written from the PowerShell source and states the call order of the author wrapper, the
  appended-run rule, replace_text, resolve_revisions, fill_template, the table lookups and the refusal texts. tests/fixtures/word-edit/ holds only the input
  the scenarios copy (inputs/pixel.png) because no recording could be made here (no Word): run `node recorder/record-office-com.mjs --area word-edit` on the
  migration PC, then the call logs cut at the operation markers are to be replayed against `Editor` (the test file has the manifest check for them; the replay
  itself is not written, since the recorded steps' format has no sample in the tree yet). The scenario file is checked to name every one of the 41 operations.
- One order differs from the PowerShell host by necessity: `fill_template` visits the token variants of a story in order of their first appearance in its text; the
  PowerShell host visited them in .NET hashtable key order, which cannot be reproduced. Nothing but the order of the keys of `filled` can show it.
- The arithmetic of the natural column widths of add_table (the unsized-table branch) is done in single and double precision as the script's operand types decide
  (page width minus margins in single, the sum of the columns in double); the replay of the recorded `Width` puts will show a difference if PowerShell used double
  throughout.
